Preparing for a DevOps, SRE, or Cloud Engineer interview?

Based on my experience on both sides of the interview table,I've compiled a list of insightful technical questions that I hope helps you succeed in your interview
Here’s a mix of essential Linux, AWS, and Kubernetes topics you must master:

🐧 Linux & System Administration:
•Beyond RHEL:
Which Linux flavors and specific versions have you worked with in production? 
•How do you recursively search for a filename containing a specific string from the root or a sub-directory?
•What’s the modern way to find a specific string within files across an entire directory tree? 
•Explain the paradigm shift from System V init to systemd. 
•How do you verify all required services started correctly after a system reboot? How do you troubleshoot one that didn’t?

☁️ AWS & Cloud Infrastructure: 
•How do you monitor application health on an EC2 instance? Where do you check logs? 
•Compare and contrast Security Groups and NACLs. When would you use one over the other? 
•What are the primary ways to deploy a database on AWS? (Think beyond EC2!) 
•Explain the different AWS Load Balancers (ALB, NLB). Give a practical use case for each.
•What is the purpose of "sticky sessions" in load balancing?

⚙️ Kubernetes & Container Orchestration: 
•Where and how do you configure the minimum and maximum number of pods for a deployment?
•How do you check the current number of running pods and their status? 
•Walk through the lifecycle of a Pod. 
•Your pods are failing to start. What's your step-by-step troubleshooting process? 
•How does Kubernetes know when to scale up a new pod? (Hint: HPA configuration)
•Explain the difference between Secrets and ConfigMaps. How would you use a ConfigMap inside a application pod? 
•How do you securely manage database credentials in EKS/K8s? 
•Explain the concept of an Ingress controller. How would you configure routing for an application to accept external traffic?

🧠 Architecture & Design:
•How does cross-zone load balancing work, and how do you configure it?
•What critical factors do you consider when designing the infrastructure for an enterprise-grade application? 
•How do you secure traffic using Transport Layer Security (TLS) in a containerized environment?

This list is great for both self-assessment and leading team discussions to level up your squad's knowledge. 💬
